-- Forty-two example properties, so that a person opening RentMe sees what the
-- catalogue is for rather than an empty shelf.
--
-- WHAT MAKES THESE SAFE is entirely in the three migrations before this one and
-- not in this file: `is_demo` is true on every row, so the trust constraint, the
-- transaction triggers, the feed suppression and the badge suppression all
-- apply. This file's own job is narrower and is about CREDIBILITY rather than
-- safety: the data has to be right, because a Nigerian reader spots invented
-- property data instantly and the fastest tell is a price that does not match
-- its area.
--
-- THE RULES THE DATA FOLLOWS.
--
-- Areas are real and prices are area-appropriate: an Ikoyi three-bedroom at
-- 18m a year and a Bodija two-bedroom at 900k a year are both plausible, and
-- swapping them would be obvious to anybody who lives in either.
--
-- Coordinates are real points inside the named area, scattered by a few hundred
-- metres so pins do not stack on one spot. `listings_location_sync` derives the
-- PostGIS geography from them, so these land on `listings_location_gist` and
-- answer `listings_in_bounds` properly. No pin is in the lagoon.
--
-- ADDRESS IS NULL ON EVERY ROW, DELIBERATELY. A street address on an invented
-- property is somebody's actual house, with strangers being told they can rent
-- it. That is a different category of problem from a marketing embarrassment.
-- The area, the city and an approximate pin are the whole location claim.
--
-- Light and water are the point of this catalogue, not decoration. Nigeria is
-- the market and power band, generator hours, water source and prepaid metering
-- are what a person actually decides on. They are varied honestly and roughly a
-- quarter of these properties are genuinely poorly served: PATCHY or RARELY on
-- the grid, no backup at all, water by tanker. A shelf where every property is
-- Band A with a solar inverter is obviously fabricated, and it would also
-- misrepresent the country.
--
-- No row carries a rating, a review, a view count or a save count. Those are
-- not omitted here for tidiness; they are structurally impossible, because
-- `reviews.booking_id` is NOT NULL and a booking against one of these rows is
-- refused by trigger.

insert into public.listings (
  id, agent_id, title, description, property_type, status, is_demo,
  state_code, city, area, address, latitude, longitude,
  bedrooms, bathrooms, toilets, parking_spaces, floor, total_floors,
  size_sqm, year_built, condition, furnished,
  listing_intent, rent_amount_minor, rent_period, rent_negotiable,
  caution_deposit_minor, service_charge_minor, service_charge_period,
  agency_fee_minor, legal_fee_minor, agreement_fee_minor, minimum_tenancy_months,
  rate_minor, rate_period,
  sale_price_minor, price_negotiable, tenure, sale_status,
  power_grid, power_backup, power_backup_hours, water_supply, prepaid_meter,
  has_estate_access, available_from, published_at
) values
